Mechanics and Design: Mechanics were building a mock field for the robot to practice on, and building the robot's chassis.

Design was prototyping plywood models of some of the robot's mechanisms and tinkering on CAD.

![](https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/meips/ADKq_NZZ0D4n8wM1It2xz4PG_cdHPfPCPlppRd71N62O5CZHs_kpdoPK2Mntuns1PaxaQ_6IhVMFdRT7EK3NUE1IqWmTVzHd5dSzNky5WBkbWtPG1fzYcud7BIyEe-MGX4pQBJS-8e-JSmD5VJ_3QPp8pcBNHDw_MK7LfU0=s0-d-e1-ft#https://mcusercontent.com/83401ef6f6634dd529783840a/images/d03a5354-317f-03cd-1af1-a719684b3edd.jpg)

Programming: Programming worked on the swerve drive code for this year, messed with the robot's "vision", and played with LED strips.

![](https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/meips/ADKq_NYuP7RjqEQFLYGgpmTVhAnUiBNi2qSaBAlrHe8j_65hXaXWLJI7OXP5MrGWWFB_WNCk9fzYkfrjUVmQrK7EsfWldsmAV31fxpypSyd6oymhQuJBoyM2BA74ejZZFN0Sjd0rfluf02PkDDRy733hKYWoCNY08n3tFrE=s0-d-e1-ft#https://mcusercontent.com/83401ef6f6634dd529783840a/images/fe15b958-fe59-2697-3a7c-d0d3b6fa4e6c.jpg)

Electronics/Pneumatics:

Electronics raced to wire swerve modules (which control robot movement), and worked with the new motor.

![](https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/meips/ADKq_NbwcOI91a11KyDzBqR5LfxYLDkkZ58bu9ij9OFfQ1ICaT59K80_cNpZfaPEKl-B10X265nuvaV8iFlu3mTmuoQj6dxOBy9CouPhJmAGTn3DMyWC_69yC0YxobaoXavgw89Wxf-C6KcWXW48NzldQg6z1drJAeKCQb4=s0-d-e1-ft#https://mcusercontent.com/83401ef6f6634dd529783840a/images/d7d05cf8-6fdd-e506-4fa5-7b1fdb6e5dc7.jpg)

Business + Marketing:

Our team set up the Spartronics Pit where our robot will be worked on during competitions. We also wrote the newsletter.  

